{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-39767",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "Remember that we can factor a constant out of the norm, provided that we take the absolute value of the constant:\n\n$$\n‖kx‖=|k|\\cdot ‖x‖\n$$\n\nUsing this fact and the formula for the norm, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖-3x‖ & =|-3|\\cdot ‖x‖ \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}+{x}_{4}^{2}+{x}_{5}^{2}} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{(-9)^{2}+(\\sqrt{11})^{2}+{0}^{2}+(-5)^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{81+11+0+25+4} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{121} \\\\  & =3\\cdot 11 \\\\  & =33.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
